    "reference": "Abruptly discontinuing or decreasing nicotine intake results in nicotine withdrawal symptoms. These symptoms include cravings, anger, irritability, anxiety, depression, impatience, trouble sleeping, restlessness, increased hunger, and difficulty concentrating. Nicotine withdrawal is recognized by the American Psychiatric Association and the WHO."
